  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Engineer's Study, Drawn in a Workbook",
    "overview": "\n**Creative North Star: \"The Engineer's Study, Drawn in a Workbook\"**\n\nThe site is a workbook: printed text in a calm column, and next to it things drawn by hand. What is drawn is the furniture of a study. The library is a bookcase with nightstands beside it, the tech radar is an instrument with a round scope and a knob, the race calendar is a row of paper bibs pinned by their corners. Each is drawn the way an engineer sketches: a projection that is actually constructed, a contour, a label in handwriting. A drawing here explains or holds content; none is decoration.\n\nTwo states are recorded in this file. Today the hand lives only inside the drawn modules and inlined drawings, and everything else (header, navigation, headings, the reading column) is the stock Quartz theme. The direction is that the hand enters the frame too: section openers, the header, navigation. The reading column stays typeset in both states.\n\n- Text is typeset, objects are drawn. A module is an object from the study before it is a widget.\n- Pencil for structure, marker for what carries meaning.\n- Handwriting (Caveat) for anything written on a drawn object.\n- Flat page. Depth comes from drawn projection, never from shadows on the page.\n- The hand is reproducible: strokes are generated from a seed and baked into paths.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Text is typeset, objects are drawn. A module is an object from the study before it is a widget.",
      "Pencil for structure, marker for what carries meaning.",
      "Handwriting (Caveat) for anything written on a drawn object.",
      "Flat page. Depth comes from drawn projection, never from shadows on the page.",
      "The hand is reproducible: strokes are generated from a seed and baked into paths."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Pencil Follows the Theme Rule",
        "body": "Pencil strokes use the page's text colour and sit on the page's ground. Marker and paper keep their own colours in light and dark.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Done Rule",
        "body": "Marker red is spent on commitment and completion, plus the mark itself. It is not an accent for links, buttons or headings.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Written-On Rule",
        "body": "Caveat appears where something is written on a drawn object or, in the direction above, on the frame. Running text is never set in it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Drawn Depth Rule",
        "body": "A module shows depth by construction and hatching. A box-shadow on a card or a panel is not part of this system.",
        "section": "elevation"
